@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@
+# Administrator entry and RealYu branding
+
+The RealYu operator requested direct use after login on 2026-10-10. The native first-use acknowledgement dialog and its route/API interception are therefore detached from the active application. This is a product behavior change, not an automatic acceptance: no consent/acknowledgement record is created, existing records are not edited, and the original legal documents and project attribution remain available.
+
+Administrator JWT/API-key authentication, database role/status checks, revoked-token checks, audit middleware, rate limits and sensitive-action step-up checks remain in place. The normal admin, admin payment and admin page routes all retain their original authentication. Ordinary users do not become native administrators.
+
+## Explicit branding seed after the reviewed rollout
+
+`brand-settings.json` is an explicit five-field native settings payload. It is not a startup default and must not be applied on every service boot. It changes only `site_name`, `site_logo`, `site_subtitle`, `api_base_url` and `frontend_url`.
+
+1. Confirm the intended native production release is ACTIVE and the installed binary matches its reviewed pin. Preserve the current five settings and their absent/present state before updating them.
+2. Authenticate through the normal native login using the existing administrator credentials. Keep credentials and JWT only in memory/private runtime tooling.
+3. Send the payload using authenticated `PUT /api/v1/admin/settings`. The native partial-update implementation leaves omitted fields unchanged and runs its normal HTML-cache invalidation callback. Do not call `/admin/compliance/accept` or insert an acknowledgement record.
+4. Verify all five intended values in the authenticated settings response. `GET /api/v1/settings/public` exposes the four public brand/API fields; `frontend_url` remains an administrator setting. Fetch a new HTML page and verify its injected config has the same brand. The native embedded HTML cache has no TTL; direct SQL alone cannot complete this update. Do not restart a second time when the normal settings API succeeds.
+5. Open a fresh browser context, log in and verify the native console, RealYu logo and `/teams` navigation. Existing open tabs may require a page reload to replace their Pinia settings cache.
+
+The exact logo `/brand/realyu-wordmark.png` activates the existing RealYu CSS, favicon and team-menu feature gate. The asset is already embedded. The endpoint origin is `https://api.realyu.fun`; native client guides derive `/v1` when required. No account, API key, subscription, payment configuration or ledger value belongs in this branding payload.
+
+Before the first production repair, a read-only query of the ACTIVE r3 generation on 2026-10-10 20:37:15 Beijing time found these five keys absent. Private evidence was saved as `brand-settings-before-20261010T123715Z.json`. Initial real browser login was successful but had the old acknowledgement prompt and no team menu; those first results/screenshots are preserved privately rather than overwritten.
+
+## Separate follow-ups
+
+Old `RegisterEnabled=true` was observed, while native `registration_enabled` and `realyu_username_registration_enabled` were absent/false. Restore that parity only as a separately reviewed native setting change, with its registration/grant behavior understood; the branding seed does not silently open registration or promise migrated welcome credit.
+
+Both legacy installer downloads remain under `/downloads/realyu/`. Native infrastructure `/setup/status` is already completed. Do not add a fake setup URL or point users at removed New API routes. Customer currency formatting is a separate change; model reference prices and the internal monetary ledger must not be changed by branding.
+
+## Focused acceptance
+
+The focused regression uses the real route registration and real JWT validation for the native admin settings, admin payment config and admin page list. It covers a valid administrator with no acknowledgement record, anonymous/invalid tokens, an ordinary member, a disabled administrator and a revoked administrator token. It asserts no acknowledgement lookup/write is required. Frontend tests exercise the actual App mount, actual registered navigation guard, and API error interceptor: the route renders without a prompt or consent call, while anonymous/member navigation is still refused.
+
+These local tests do not themselves prove the new production binary or public browser was updated. Final release evidence must name the deployed build and repeat the public browser checks after the normal settings update.
