+# RealYu single-core team and client compatibility
+
+These additions use native Sub2API authentication, PostgreSQL, model routing and
+Vue. They do not run a second New API channel manager. The legacy source contract
+comes from the RealYu new-api fork (QuantumNous attribution retained), delivered
+at `93357b11481e7dd7c1811870c455968151d23474`.
+
+## Team API and UI
+
+`/teams` is a native authenticated Vue route. Its sidebar entry is visible for the
+RealYu logo. The backend feature is enabled only by `REALYU_FUNDING_ENABLED`.
+Every call reads the authenticated actor's current database status and team scope;
+UI visibility is not the authorization boundary.
+
+| Endpoint under `/api/v1/realyu/teams` | Behavior |
+| --- | --- |
+| `GET /` | Accessible teams only |
+| `GET /:team_id` | Current team allowance and members; ordinary members see themselves |
+| `PATCH /:team_id` | Owner/authorized administrator renames team |
+| `PUT /:team_id/members/:member_id` | Change weekly cap or `active`/`disabled`/`removed` state |
+| `GET /:team_id/usage` | Member/model/date filters, consistent page/total/statistics/breakdown |
+| `POST /:team_id/invite` | Rotate invite; store SHA-256 only, return new code once |
+| `POST /join` | Join by invite; provision a native scoped team key, initial cap 0 |
+| `POST /:team_id/leave` | Member leaves and team keys are retired |
+
+Owners and native administrators can manage their authorized teams. Migrated
+role 10 may manage teams belonging to lower-role users, without native admin
+privileges. It cannot manage native admin/peer role 10 owners or elevated target
+members. Role 10's old global user/personal-funding administration is not included
+here; native administrator functionality remains unchanged.
+
+Usage `start`/`end` are RFC3339 with an exclusive end; one request covers at most
+31 days. `page_size` is 1–100. The UI accepts an inclusive end date and converts it
+to the next day's boundary. Ordinary members cannot read another member's usage.
+New consumption joins native usage logs to settled funding requests by request
+and key, and excludes personal usage. Historical actors without current member
+rows appear as read-only former members. Names are labels; authorization uses IDs.
+
+USD values retain the existing 500,000 quota/USD conversion. Caps are spending
+limits, never transfers to personal balances. Disabling/removing members prevents
+future admissions but does not undo already admitted consumption. Lowering a cap
+does not reset the member's used quota. The API intentionally does not create new
+team products or new team subscriptions. Switching teams requires explicit leave
+before join; there is no silent transfer of funding or keys.
+
+## Sealed historical import
+
+Run native schema migrations through **305** before importing. First complete the
+main `singlecore_migrate.py` customer import with a sealed, consistent SQLite S1
+backup. Then run `import_team_history.py` against that same SHA-256 and target.
+
+```powershell
+$snapshot = 'C:\migration\customer-s1.db'
+$sha = (Get-FileHash -LiteralPath $snapshot -Algorithm SHA256).Hash.ToLowerInvariant()
+& 'C:\runtime\venv\Scripts\python.exe' .\deploy\realyu\import_team_history.py --source $snapshot --sha256 $sha
+& 'C:\runtime\venv\Scripts\python.exe' .\deploy\realyu\import_team_history.py --source $snapshot --sha256 $sha --private-target 'C:\private\migration-target.json' --apply --report 'C:\migration\team-history-result.json'
+```
+
+The private JSON uses the main importer's `host`, `port`, `database`, `user`,
+`password`, `installation_id` and `mode` fields. Host must be loopback; mode must
+be `rehearsal` or `staging`. The persisted installation, phase and customer
+snapshot hash must all match. Any new native usage/funding/team audit writes block
+the import. Source access is immutable/read-only, hash-checked before and after,
+and rejects WAL/journal sidecars. Use a SQLite backup, never a live database file.
+
+Historical scope follows the deployed old code: `workspace_team_id=-1` is
+personal; positive IDs preserve the explicit team; zero IDs need the old
+owner/credential-holder relationship and a timestamp after team creation. Soft
+deleted tokens remain available for attribution. Missing source teams are stored
+in `realyu_legacy_team_usage_orphans` with original IDs and a reason; they are not
+assigned to current customers. Existing-team actor/owner mismatches fail the
+import. Error/refund diagnostic logs are not consumption rows and remain in the
+sealed original snapshot. Unattributed zero-scope rows are counted separately.
+
+No balances, caps, weekly used amounts or paid-order states change. History and
+invite hashes commit together with an import receipt. Repeating a completed
+snapshot is a no-op. Do not activate traffic until the main and historical
+receipts are reconciled. The importer refuses an `active` target.
+
+## Existing installer and monitoring URLs
+
+Set these variables in the native service's private environment:
+
+| Variable | Meaning/default |
+| --- | --- |
+| `REALYU_CLIENT_ASSETS_DIR` | Absolute directory containing the sealed existing `web/public/downloads/realyu` contents; empty disables downloads |
+| `REALYU_CLIENT_DIAGNOSTICS_DIR` | Absolute private writable diagnostic directory; empty disables collection |
+
+Keep the assets directory read-only to the service account. Copy the whole
+existing directory, including `runtime`, manifests and the roughly 32 MB client;
+do not regenerate installers or add binaries to a source patch. Verify each
+manifest's existing checksums after copying. Static GET/HEAD at
+`/downloads/realyu/*file` preserve byte ranges, original Content-Length and
+`no-transform`. Bootstrap scripts are not cached; executable/tar bundles retain
+the old cache policy. Missing files return 404, not the SPA. `os.OpenRoot` confines
+access, and backslash/alternate data stream paths are rejected.
+
+`POST /api/client/diagnostics` preserves the old report-field allowlist, 4 KiB
+body cap, 120 reports/minute/IP, 5,000-file maximum and 30-day retention. Unknown
+fields are discarded. Client claims are marked `unverified_client`; reports do
+not accept raw logs, paths, exception messages or arbitrary credentials. Only
+durably persisted/deduplicated reports receive 202. A disabled/broken sink returns
+503. Redis failure closes this anonymous write endpoint rather than accepting an
+unlimited stream. Restrict diagnostic directory access to the service/operator.
+
+`GET /api/status` returns legacy `success`, `data.version` and `data.system_name`
+plus `engine=sub2api`. Success requires a bounded native PostgreSQL and Redis
+ping. It is a dependency check, not evidence that a paid upstream model works.
+
+## Receive-only old payment notifications
+
+`REALYU_LEGACY_PAYMENT_ENABLED` defaults to false. When deliberately enabled,
+provide the **old** merchant configuration through private
+`REALYU_LEGACY_PAYMENT_MERCHANT_ID`, `REALYU_LEGACY_PAYMENT_MERCHANT_KEY` and
+`REALYU_LEGACY_PAYMENT_GATEWAY_URL` variables. Do not put these in Git or output.
+
+Old billing/subscription notify URLs retain GET and POST:
+`/api/billing/epay/notify` and `/api/subscription/epay/notify`. A provider `success`
+means the verified event was durably received, not that it was fulfilled.
+`pending_review` needs reconciliation. Unknown/mismatched orders fail; there is
+no fabricated old return-page fulfillment success.
+
+## Validation and current limits (2026-10-10)
+
+- Frontend: 22 focused tests (10 team component, 2 exact quota, 10 sidebar),
+  `vue-tsc --noEmit` and scoped ESLint passed with pnpm 9.15.9.
+- Team repository: 6 actual PostgreSQL tests passed using random isolated schemas;
+  team HTTP contract tests: 4 roots passed. Native server compilation passed.
+- History importer: 6 contract + 5 actual PostgreSQL tests passed. Tests verify
+  no balance writes, idempotence, scope, rollback and active-target rejection.
+- Installer/status/diagnostics: 5 handler roots passed, 1 symlink-creation test
+  skipped because this Windows host lacks symlink creation privileges. The
+  `os.Root` implementation is still used. Embedded-frontend bypass test passed.
+- S0 read-only inspection: 25,767 consume rows; 20,126 current-team rows; 5,208
+  personal/preteam exclusions; 429 unattributed zero-scope; 4 missing-team
+  quarantines; 3 active invites. One error/refund diagnostic row is outside the
+  consumption view. These counts must be recomputed for S1.
+- Running candidate HTTP acceptance on `127.0.0.1:29480` against the disposable
+  `realyu_singlecore_e2e` database: 60 recorded checks, 57 passed (53 JSON API
+  checks and 4 embedded HTML routes), 3 administrator checks reached the native
+  first-use acknowledgement gate. Fresh synthetic owner/member/role-10 accounts
+  exercised cross-team denial, own-only usage, date and pagination consistency,
+  exact caps, state changes, invite rotation, joining and leaving. No upstream
+  model calls or production writes were made by this acceptance pass.
+
+The native administrator accounts, usage and dashboard endpoints return
+`423 ADMIN_COMPLIANCE_ACK_REQUIRED` until that administrator handles the
+upstream console's first-use prompt. Keep that original interaction; do not seed
+an acknowledgement on a real operator's behalf. It is not a team migration
+failure. The three administrator checks must be rerun after normal confirmation.
+
+These are isolated repository/component and actual candidate HTTP checks plus a
+read-only customer snapshot inspection. Browser inventory was empty; both IAB
+and Chrome control returned unavailable. No browser rendering, UI interaction,
+or production deployment is claimed here. A later, separate real-upstream WS
+acceptance is described below. Synthetic acceptance credentials remain
+only in the private runtime folder, and this disposable database must not become
+the production S1 target.
+
+The WS review found no new scope bypass in fresh-key reads, allowed-group preload,
+IP recompilation or signed actor/team continuation verification. Remaining P1:
+transport interruption before a terminal event may refund an unsubmitted turn
+even after partial output; passthrough's error callback supplies no per-turn
+usage. Submitted billing failures retain the reservation for reconciliation.
+Old signed response IDs prove authorization; restored Redis/account affinity
+still needs an actual old conversation continuation test.
+
+## Native WS continuation compatibility fix
+
+The first real-upstream two-turn WS test completed turn 1 but closed turn 2 with
+1008: the RealYu response-owner check could not find a binding. The original
+Sub2API `ctx_pool` path already received the correct `response.id` and put it in
+`OpenAIForwardResult.RequestID`. The added owner-binding hook reads `ResponseID`,
+which that path did not populate. The passthrough fixture had covered a different
+native ingress mode and therefore missed this integration gap.
+
+The fix adds only `ResponseID: responseID` to the existing result constructors in
+`openai_ws_forwarder_ingress.go` and `openai_ws_http_bridge.go`. It preserves
+native WS routing/continuation and all fresh-key, member, model and scope checks.
+The `ctx_pool` loop runs `AfterTurn` before parsing the next frame on the same
+connection, so that continuation sees the newly stored owner.
+
+Validation: the newly added ctx_pool continuation fixture first reproduced the
+same 1008; after the fix, passthrough and ctx_pool each passed continuation,
+revoked-key, disabled-member, forbidden-model and duplicate-model cases. HTTP
+bridge ID/continuation checks and legacy signed-response/scope checks also pass.
+
+On the isolated port 29481 candidate, the real upstream then completed both turns
+on one WS connection: handshake 101, 12 and 20 events, both exact-answer checks
+passed. Turn 2 returned the marker supplied only in turn 1. Read-only PostgreSQL
+reconciliation found two corresponding native usage/funding rows settled with
+12 and 28 quota units. This verifies this two-turn native chain; it does not
+prove migrated old response/account affinity, interruption billing or browser UI.
+
+The tested independent native binary was built from `source/backend` with:
+
+```powershell
+go build -p 2 -tags embed -ldflags '-s -w -X main.Version=realyu-singlecore-v0.2.15-20261010-ws-owner' -o 'C:\srv\realyu-singlecore-dev\runtime\sub2api-ws-owner-fix.exe' ./cmd/server
+```
+
+It embeds the already-built native frontend. SHA-256:
+`0124bffafc6232702bb43b723f21d9999e88f89e2d37b8a8261925ee7981fad9`.
+Build the frontend first when changing its sources before a final release build.
+Only the exact isolated 29481 process was replaced; production was untouched.
+
